{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564005-vtmboard-game","id":1564005,"title":"VtmBoard game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-09-13T01:57:28-07:00","id":1564005,"title":"VtmBoard game","content":"I think it would be great if we got a board game based on vtm. We did get prince of the city (based on requiem) a few years back which I really enjoyed. The base game (all about controlling sections of the city), wouldnt need to change much.Itd be great if it facilitated solo play but also allowed intrigue/elysium (not sure how compatible those last 2 are). What are peoples thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T04:13:54-07:00","id":1564009,"title":"","content":"Lots of options on what to do, the hard part is doing it.<br /> <br /> Paradox has zero built capacity in this area and a harsh reprimand still lingering from the last time outstretching their abilities cost a huge loss, so it's up to the usual channels: someone else has to take this start to finish and just ask for a license.<br /> <br /> But yeah, there's potential and there's market. Horror themed board games are an easy sell as far as boardgames go, and I can easily picture aspects of the game that can be used as basis for one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T08:24:52-07:00","id":1564014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfAsh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564005-vtmboard-game#post1564005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be great if we got a board game based on vtm. We did get prince of the city (based on requiem) a few years back which I really enjoyed. The base game (all about controlling sections of the city), wouldnt need to change much.Itd be great if it facilitated solo play but also allowed intrigue/elysium (not sure how compatible those last 2 are). What are peoples thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are multiple there already?<br /> <br /> Chapters, Blood Feud, Prince's Gambit and Milan Uprising. Rivals and Vendetta are card games (not CCGs).<br /> <br /> I don't think that is out yet but Palermo Conspiracies is made by the same company as Milan Uprising and it will be release soon (TM).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","user":"sathriel","date":". 09-13-2026, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T13:40:59-07:00","id":1564021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564005-vtmboard-game?p=1564014#post1564014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are multiple there already?<br /> <br /> Chapters, Blood Feud, Prince's Gambit and Milan Uprising. Rivals and Vendetta are card games (not CCGs).<br /> <br /> I don't think that is out yet but Palermo Conspiracies is made by the same company as Milan Uprising and it will be release soon (TM).</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think theyre board games in the traditional sense. I have Chapters for example, and its a campaign in a box, not a board game (and I still have some expansions in shrink wrap as I havent gone back to it). Prince of the city was a board game in the traditional sense IMO and I thinks theres definitely a gap there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T16:53:46-07:00","id":1564022,"title":"","content":"I don't think the &quot;traditional sense&quot; is a valid assumption anymore. Those games got pretty varied in mechanics and the actual boards and dice aren't as expected anymore, and I see no problem with that.<br /> <br /> A gap is a hard thing to point in a market that is varied, but also expensive. It's not as if making a board game were fast and cheap and a sure return.<br /> <br /> My opinion is still that the space is there, but I wouldn't frame it as a gap or something that is begging for a specific format. It's rather a matter of someone with access and resources having an idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T18:16:06-07:00","id":1564029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564005-vtmboard-game?p=1564022#post1564022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the &quot;traditional sense&quot; is a valid assumption anymore. Those games got pretty varied in mechanics and the actual boards and dice aren't as expected anymore, and I see no problem with that.<br /> <br /> A gap is a hard thing to point in a market that is varied, but also expensive. It's not as if making a board game were fast and cheap and a sure return.<br /> <br /> My opinion is still that the space is there, but I wouldn't frame it as a gap or something that is begging for a specific format. It's rather a matter of someone with access and resources having an idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hundred per cent. Just because there is a couple VtM board games does not mean there should not be more. I have not played a board game in ages and generally I'd prefer to play a game of Vampire: The Eternal Struggle anyway but I know lots of people love their board games so they serve as both a treat for people who already love Vampire and potential gateway drug for people who do not yet but they enjoy playing their board games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T08:22:12-07:00","id":1564042,"title":"","content":"hmm, seem like my response was flagged and seems stuck in 'unapproved' - copy/paste below:<br /> <br /> By traditional, I DONT mean games like monopoly etc. I play board games quite a bit and there a lot of different mechanics but there are commonalities. Also, some mechanics just work. For example, unfathomable is a lovecraftian skin for the same mechanics used in the battlestar galactica board game. They found mechanics that work and put a different theme on it. Another example is Pandemic and Fate of the Fellowship. This would make it easier for non-VTM fans to onboard too (the game could stand on its own 2 feet). In contrast, Chapters wasnt like that. Ive played through it and its more of a choose-your-own-adventure with accompanying boards, which frankly are not needed (they nailed the theme for VTM fans but I wouldnt recommend it for others).<br /> <br /> By gap, Im purely speaking to the Supply side of the argument, whether the Demand is there is another matter but this is exactly why the focus would be on making a game everyone could enjoy, with the theme acting as a hook to get more people into VTM.<br /> <br /> VTES is cool, been playing it since it came out. Its minimum 2 player though - a lot of board games have a solo option too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T09:32:01-07:00","id":1564045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfAsh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564005-vtmboard-game?p=1564042#post1564042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By traditional, I DONT mean games like monopoly etc. I play board games quite a bit and there a lot of different mechanics but there are commonalities. Also, some mechanics just work. For example, unfathomable is a lovecraftian skin for the same mechanics used in the battlestar galactica board game. They found mechanics that work and put a different theme on it. Another example is Pandemic and Fate of the Fellowship. This would make it easier for non-VTM fans to onboard too (the game could stand on its own 2 feet). In contrast, Chapters wasnt like that. Ive played through it and its more of a choose-your-own-adventure with accompanying boards, which frankly are not needed (they nailed the theme for VTM fans but I wouldnt recommend it for others).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we all understood that (may be wrong) and our points stand.<br /> <br /> Your idea of &quot;traditional&quot; board game seems to come from having quite some experience with them, but the point is that this &quot;tradition&quot; isn't as universally accepted as you think.<br /> <br /> Myself, I hate anything with long setups. I think the limit of my patience may be Diplomacy, and it's already stretching it. My problem extends to games that are &quot;traditional&quot; only as far as they have boards and pieces.<br /> <br /> So, is a &quot;traditional&quot; game something everyone will enjoy? Idk, but I wouldn't bet on it without looking at a concrete project. Have the already made games enjoyed success? It seems so.<br /> <br /> Gaps don't exist in a vacuum. Making a game or any product because you think a category must be filled is a fast lane for bad decisions. In business and development a &quot;gap&quot; means a demand going unaddressed, so by definition it can't be just &quot;this doesn't exist yet&quot;, it is &quot;there is demand or need to supply this thing that doesn't exist yet&quot;.<br /> <br /> Just to explain why I wouldn't call it a gap, what I thought you meant and that I think a more proper use of the world. Your clarification is valid and noted.<br /> <br /> But the biggest problem I tried to point is, you can't just say a certain boardgame should exist and that's it. Board game design is hard, with few professionals in the industry. You don't say it, but you want competently made rules and assets, and those take a lot of work and money to even prototype.<br /> <br /> Each board game you like is a greater initial investment than TTRPGs or videogames cause those two are more conducive of the idea of &quot;we'll think it as we do it&quot;, even if development is long and costly you can start with a rough idea and whatever.<br /> <br /> Not to say it isn't feasible. Just demanding, and that means you only have two options: either someone has a great idea and want to invest their time and effort in that particular idea, or a company pays a competent professional team to make it happen.<br /> <br /> Paradox doesn't seem interested in this for the time being, and as the IP owners they're the only ones who would do the second option. We depend entirely on the first, then, and as such on the whims of fate making a designer have an idea they want to execute with VtM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T12:33:43-07:00","id":1564050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564005-vtmboard-game?p=1564045#post1564045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we all understood that (may be wrong) and our points stand.<br /> <br /> Your idea of &quot;traditional&quot; board game seems to come from having quite some experience with them, but the point is that this &quot;tradition&quot; isn't as universally accepted as you think.<br /> <br /> Myself, I hate anything with long setups. I think the limit of my patience may be Diplomacy, and it's already stretching it. My problem extends to games that are &quot;traditional&quot; only as far as they have boards and pieces.<br /> <br /> So, is a &quot;traditional&quot; game something everyone will enjoy? Idk, but I wouldn't bet on it without looking at a concrete project. Have the already made games enjoyed success? It seems so.<br /> <br /> Gaps don't exist in a vacuum. Making a game or any product because you think a category must be filled is a fast lane for bad decisions. In business and development a &quot;gap&quot; means a demand going unaddressed, so by definition it can't be just &quot;this doesn't exist yet&quot;, it is &quot;there is demand or need to supply this thing that doesn't exist yet&quot;.<br /> <br /> Just to explain why I wouldn't call it a gap, what I thought you meant and that I think a more proper use of the world. Your clarification is valid and noted.<br /> <br /> But the biggest problem I tried to point is, you can't just say a certain boardgame should exist and that's it. Board game design is hard, with few professionals in the industry. You don't say it, but you want competently made rules and assets, and those take a lot of work and money to even prototype.<br /> <br /> Each board game you like is a greater initial investment than TTRPGs or videogames cause those two are more conducive of the idea of &quot;we'll think it as we do it&quot;, even if development is long and costly you can start with a rough idea and whatever.<br /> <br /> Not to say it isn't feasible. Just demanding, and that means you only have two options: either someone has a great idea and want to invest their time and effort in that particular idea, or a company pays a competent professional team to make it happen.<br /> <br /> Paradox doesn't seem interested in this for the time being, and as the IP owners they're the only ones who would do the second option. We depend entirely on the first, then, and as such on the whims of fate making a designer have an idea they want to execute with VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure this is helpful. At no point did I say something MUST exist, merely if people liked the idea and what they thought. No, &quot;traditional&quot; is not something everyone would enjoy but board games arent for everyone.<br /> <br /> You seem to be focusing on why it might not work, which is fine, but not what I was asking about. As neither of us (correct me if Im wrong) are in the board games business, we cant speak to numbers. I can say there are plenty of board games out there though and it doesnt have to be as big a gamble with options like reskinning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T00:54:45-07:00","id":1564070,"title":"","content":"You asked thoughts. Those are my thoughts. Pondering feasibility is one thing I like to do. For me at least, just saying &quot;would be cool&quot; without adding anything is what isn't helpful or interesting, and I don't personally have any idea of what to do as such a game.<br /> <br /> I can't make a board game happen, I can't say how it should be, I can though analyze possible causes for it not currently existing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfAsh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564005-vtmboard-game?p=1564050#post1564050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, &quot;traditional&quot; is not something everyone would enjoy but board games arent for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting turn of phrase.<br /> <br /> But as the marketing has been catering to a broader audience now, including a lot of people with no interest in &quot;traditional&quot;, and everyone still agrees to call it board games, I think this may not be a dominant thesis at the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfAsh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564005-vtmboard-game?p=1564050#post1564050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As neither of us (correct me if Im wrong) are in the board games business, we cant speak to numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in the marketing analysis business, and as an amateur but enthusiast board/TTRPG game developer I have some idea of how it works, so take from that what you may.<br /> <br /> Part of the fun of discussing in the internet is that you never know what other participants do actually work with, so any assumption is quite risky, including of ignorance.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think I'll later hit my sources on how is the temperature of the market right now and the appetite for classic IPs horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T08:12:10-07:00","id":1564082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564005-vtmboard-game?p=1564070#post1564070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You asked thoughts. Those are my thoughts. Pondering feasibility is one thing I like to do. For me at least, just saying &quot;would be cool&quot; without adding anything is what isn't helpful or interesting, and I don't personally have any idea of what to do as such a game.<br /> <br /> I can't make a board game happen, I can't say how it should be, I can though analyze possible causes for it not currently existing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Interesting turn of phrase.<br /> <br /> But as the marketing has been catering to a broader audience now, including a lot of people with no interest in &quot;traditional&quot;, and everyone still agrees to call it board games, I think this may not be a dominant thesis at the moment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm in the marketing analysis business, and as an amateur but enthusiast board/TTRPG game developer I have some idea of how it works, so take from that what you may.<br /> <br /> Part of the fun of discussing in the internet is that you never know what other participants do actually work with, so any assumption is quite risky, including of ignorance.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think I'll later hit my sources on how is the temperature of the market right now and the appetite for classic IPs horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Id certainly be curious to hear the results of that analysis, given your background. I would suggest not focusing too much on the horror aspect though. Theme is very important in board games of course, but if the game mechanics are good (and the presentation is not horrific) then I think it wont be a problem. There is a cthulu skin for pandemic for example.<br /> <br /> In terms of thoughts, 'I dont think it would work because of X, Y Z' is fair enough but we seem to be getting into to the weeds on it without having access to the data. Also, there are a huge number of board games out there and a lot, maybe even most, dont have established IPs to fall back on. This is where Im coming from when I say the focus could be on making the game good first.<br /> In terms of peoples thoughts, Id like to hear what people thought worked/didnt work in prince of the city and what aspects of VTM would work. Im not that interested in discussing whether it would work or not as<br /> A) Im not pitching this is an idea to Paradox so who cares whats discussed here.<br /> B) Im confident that with the right gameplay design that it would do OK at least, given whats available in the market already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1440,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","user":"LordOfAsh","date":". 09-15-2026, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T10:35:50-07:00","id":1564087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfAsh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564005-vtmboard-game?p=1564082#post1564082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Id certainly be curious to hear the results of that analysis, given your background.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's where your definition of &quot;traditional&quot; matter a lot, because it may be clear in your head, but isn't in general. There's no avoiding it, you'll have to be specific and not assume other people know what you're talking about, as even the seemingly most obvious reference may be far more regional than you think and this is an international forum.<br /> <br /> Long story short, the market is going well, very well, and the parts of it where Vampire sits are growing above average. The public want to see more games that aren't for children, to enjoy a beloved IP and to dive into a more thematic experience.<br /> <br /> But, &quot;traditional&quot; isn't a word I'd associate with the trends in design. Videogames are a strong competitor and they're absorbing the demand for competitive play and some others you may see as traditional. The appetite for novelty not only in skin, but mechanics, is high.<br /> <br /> There's also the strict business side you don't want to know, but is where we can see if what you want has a chance to appear. You only see the public-facing result of successful (at least marginally) games, not the machine that produced it, but the machine is what produces it.<br /> <br /> IPs are on the rise. For kids. By big companies. This is expected. They put their money where a good return is expected. They won't enter a license deal that isn't really good, and VtM isn't juicy enough to work at their scale yet, not for a reskin of something with appeal to children.<br /> <br /> We do have good prospects in general for this IP, and we already got a partnership with WotC, so I'd say new titles coming is actually very likely.<br /> <br /> Just not as reskin of more traditional titles. The trends in several directions point to something like Vampire clinging to more narrative co-op rules, with plenty novelty and mixing digital in the experience.<br /> <br /> Other than that, do you have any ideas on the mechanics and aspects of the game you'd like to see in a game? I think an asymmetrical game pitching the Prince or Primogen against the local Anarch factions could be something, a battle where the stakes are how much you get to decide policy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T12:30:41-07:00","id":1564092,"title":"","content":"<br /> Not sure where kids come into it - in the community Im looking at its mostly adults (of all ages) that get into it. A lot of these things are quite expensive.<br /> <br /> In terms of gameplay, prince of the citys board as the city divided into sectors that be controlled. Each clan had access to abilities that helped controlling these sectors or did other things (bonuses to attack for example). There was also a deck of cards to give bonuses. It was competitive and the only thing I didnt like was that the player score was tracked in public. Not really in line with the setting IMO and just meant the other players would gang up on the leader near the end of the game.<br /> <br /> A Co-op could definitely work. A coterie working together to fight off some threat. For example, with fate of the fellowship (which supports solo play, expand the consumer net I think), objectives are cards drawn from a deck and can vary between games. Enemy movements/actions are entirely controlled by a deck from which cards are drawn. Pitching prince/primogen against anarchs could be one objective, fighing off the sabbat could be another, locking down the masquerade etc.<br /> <br /> Id keep an open mind regarding digital experience - only exposure I have to that is mansions of madness. Excellent game but it only comes with 4 scenarios, with the rest requiring purchasing. Might not be specific to digital but then again the medium might encourage this type of 'dlc' thinking. Cool so long as the initial purchase comes with a decent amount of scenarios.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T17:10:32-07:00","id":1564103,"title":"","content":"Kids come into understanding where the money is going, and this community highlights the problem of talking only from personal experience. Different ways of looking for board games and players will surface different segments.<br /> <br /> Children are the lion's share of the board game market. There are several reasons for this from gift-giving culture to parents that need to include the whole family. One important caveat is that usually a game will be classified by the youngest audience supported, so you can see a lot of games who are loved by adults classed as for children.<br /> <br /> As a result, games for children are where the big gaming companies are willing to place the bulk of their investments, and seek IPs that can help improve sales. Other markets will receive less attention and effort. And that's us.<br /> <br /> That's why everything has a Star Wars version, a Marvel, a Dr Who and so on. It's not just that those are famous IPs, but crucially they make for games a parent don't have to chose if they'll treat themselves or their children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}